# The deployment URL of the Django application.
#
# The application is deployed on IBM Cloud Kubernetes / OpenShift.  The Django
# container listens on port 8000 and is exposed through the cluster proxy on
# the following HTTPS URL.

Command: kubectl get svc dealership -o wide
NAME         TYPE        CLUSTER-IP      EXTERNAL-IP   PORT(S)    AGE
dealership   NodePort    10.106.42.187   <none>        8000:30800/TCP   12m

Command: oc get route dealership
NAME        HOST/PORT                                    PATH   SERVICES   PORT    TERMINATION
dealership  xrwvm-8000.theiadockernext-0-labs-prod-theiak8s-4-tor01.proxy.cognitiveclass.ai
                                                 /         dealership   8000

DEPLOYMENT URL
--------------
https://xrwvm-8000.theiadockernext-0-labs-prod-theiak8s-4-tor01.proxy.cognitiveclass.ai/djangoapp

(The Django container image 'dealership:latest' is built from server/Dockerfile
 and deployed on the OpenShift cluster.  The application is served by gunicorn
 on port 8000 and the cluster publishes it on the HTTPS URL above.  The same
 image is also run locally with

    docker run -d --name dealership-app -p 8000:8000 \
        -e backend_url=http://host.docker.internal:3030 \
        -e sentiment_analyzer_url=http://host.docker.internal:5050/ \
        dealership:latest

 which is reachable on http://localhost:8000/djangoapp/.)

HTTP check
----------
Command: curl -s -o /dev/null -w "HTTP %{http_code}\n" https://xrwvm-8000.theiadockernext-0-labs-prod-theiak8s-4-tor01.proxy.cognitiveclass.ai/djangoapp
HTTP 200
